	spec: '/queue <prompt> queues a prompt for the current session like Alt-Enter; /queue lists queued prompts, numbered; /queue next moves the oldest queued prompt to run now (as steering if a turn runs, else as a new turn); /queue clear drops them all and says how many. /send <target> <message> sends a prompt to exactly one other session like the send tool, where target is a tab number or a session id; an unknown target (including "all") is refused with the reason, and a message starting with / runs as a command there (so "/send 3 /rename Review" renames tab 3). There is no /broadcast or /send all command. Tests: queue, list, next and clear; /send to a tab number and to an id; /send of a command; an unknown target; no multi-recipient delivery.',
